, {"w": "Tuesday", "t": 461.66}, {"w": "afternoon", "t": 461.88}, {"w": "when", "t": 462.56}, {"w": "nobody", "t": 463.2}, {"w": "is", "t": 463.52}, {"w": "watching.", "t": 463.86}, {"w": "The", "t": 465.02}, {"w": "good", "t": 465.62}, {"w": "news?", "t": 465.78}, {"w": "Every", "t": 466.76}, {"w": "single", "t": 467.04}, {"w": "term", "t": 467.56}, {"w": "is", "t": 468.12}, {"w": "trainable.", "t": 468.62}, {"w": "So", "t": 471.48}, {"w": "here's", "t": 472.16}, {"w": "the", "t": 472.46}, {"w": "bottom", "t": 472.54}, {"w": "line", "t": 472.74}, {"w": "of", "t": 473.08}, {"w": "this", "t": 473.2}, {"w": "lesson.", "t": 473.32}, {"w": "And", "t": 474.26}, {"w": "it's", "t": 474.28}, {"w": "the", "t": 474.38}, {"w": "mindset", "t": 474.52}, {"w": "shift", "t": 474.86}, {"w": "that", "t": 475.34}, {"w": "separates", "t": 475.8}, {"w": "the", "t": 476.22}, {"w": "10", "t": 476.52}, {"w": "%", "t": 476.78}, {"w": "from", "t": 477.14}, {"w": "the", "t": 477.78}, {"w": "90.", "t": 477.94}, {"w": "Successful", "t": 479.82}, {"w": "traders", "t": 480.5}, {"w": "focus", "t": 480.8}, {"w": "on", "t": 481.22}, {"w": "the", "t": 481.66}, {"w": "process,", "t": 481.82}, {"w": "not", "t": 482.94}, {"w": "on", "t": 483.26}, {"w": "a", "t": 483.64}, {"w": "single", "t": 483.74}, {"w": "trade.", "t": 483.96}, {"w": "One", "t": 485.42}, {"w": "trade", "t": 485.6}, {"w": "means", "t": 485.94}, {"w": "nothing.", "t": 486.48}, {"w": "It's", "t": 487.7}, {"w": "noise.", "t": 487.82}, {"w": "A", "t": 489.0}, {"w": "hundred", "t": 489.02}, {"w": "trades", "t": 489.4}, {"w": "executed", "t": 489.92}, {"w": "by", "t": 490.46}, {"w": "the", "t": 490.92}, {"w": "same", "t": 491.04}, {"w": "clean", "t": 491.34}, {"w": "system.", "t": 491.64}, {"w": "That's", "t": 492.98}, {"w": "a", "t": 493.36}, {"w": "business.", "t": 493.44}, {"w": "Build", "t": 495.24}, {"w": "the", "t": 495.24}, {"w": "system.", "t": 495.46}, {"w": "Follow", "t": 496.46}, {"w": "the", "t": 496.58}, {"w": "system.", "t": 496.84}, {"w": "Review", "t": 497.82}, {"w": "the", "t": 497.9}, {"w": "system.", "t": 498.5}, {"w": "Do", "t": 499.44}, {"w": "that", "t": 499.78}, {"w": "and", "t": 500.18}, {"w": "the", "t": 500.76}, {"w": "results", "t": 500.88}, {"w": "stop", "t": 501.1}, {"w": "being", "t": 501.54}, {"w": "luck", "t": 501.88}, {"w": "and", "t": 502.14}, {"w": "start", "t": 502.76}, {"w": "being", "t": 503.1}, {"w": "math.", "t": 503.58}, {"w": "In", "t": 505.42}, {"w": "the", "t": 505.88}, {"w": "next", "t": 505.98}, {"w": "lesson,", "t": 506.2}, {"w": "we", "t": 507.04}, {"w": "begin", "t": 507.1}, {"w": "building", "t": 507.4}, {"w": "exactly", "t": 507.82}, {"w": "that", "t": 508.2}, {"w": "system.", "t": 508.72}, {"w": "Starting", "t": 509.66}, {"w": "with", "t": 509.94}, {"w": "the", "t": 510.34}, {"w": "question,", "t": 510.44}, {"w": "what", "t": 511.5}, {"w": "is", "t": 511.78}, {"w": "retail", "t": 512.12}, {"w": "money?", "t": 512.52}, {"w": "And", "t": 513.78}, {"w": "why", "t": 513.8}, {"w": "does", "t": 514.04}, {"w": "the", "t": 514.22}, {"w": "market", "t": 514.36}, {"w": "know", "t": 514.66}, {"w": "exactly", "t": 514.92}, {"w": "where", "t": 515.22}, {"w": "it", "t": 515.74}, {"w": "sits?", "t": 515.88}, {"w": "See", "t": 517.12}, {"w": "you", "t": 517.32}, {"w": "there.", "t": 517.5}], "segs": [{"t": 0.0, "txt": "What's up, traders? Welcome back to the Academy."}, {"t": 3.32, "txt": "Today's lesson is the one nobody likes to hear and everybody needs."}, {"t": 8.02, "txt": "Why most traders lose money? We'll break down the exact mistakes that empty"}, {"t": 12.56, "txt": "accounts so you can skip every single one of them."}, {"t": 16.18, "txt": "Let's get into it. Welcome back to the Academy."}, {"t": 19.8, "txt": "Today's lesson is the one most courses skip because it doesn't sell well."}, {"t": 24.3, "txt": "Why most traders lose money? And I want to be completely honest with you here"}, {"t": 29.3, "txt": "because if you understand why the majority fails,"}, {"t": 32.78, "txt": "you already know half of what you need to end up on the other side of that statistic."}, {"t": 37.66, "txt": "So let's rip the Band-Aid off."}, {"t": 42.38, "txt": "Let's start with the numbers because they are brutal."}, {"t": 45.86, "txt": "Across brokers and regulators, the data keeps landing in the same range."}, {"t": 50.5, "txt": "80 to 90 percent of retail traders lose money."}, {"t": 54.64, "txt": "Think about that. Out of every 10 people who open a trading account,"}, {"t": 58.26, "txt": "maybe one or two survive long term."}, {"t": 62.0, "txt": "Most of them fail within their first one or two years."}, {"t": 65.66, "txt": "But here's the part that should actually make you optimistic."}, {"t": 68.92, "txt": "When you study how they lose, it's almost never bad luck."}, {"t": 73.3, "txt": "It's the same handful of mistakes repeated over and over."}, {"t": 77.48, "txt": "And mistakes that repeat in a pattern are mistakes you can avoid."}, {"t": 83.26, "txt": "So before we go further, write this one sentence down"}, {"t": 86.92, "txt": "because it's the foundation for everything that follows."}, {"t": 91.0, "txt": "The majority doesn't lose because of the market."}, {"t": 93.9, "txt": "The market doesn't hunt beginners."}, {"t": 96.86, "txt": "They lose because of their own decisions."}, {"t": 99.78, "txt": "Decisions made without a plan, without rules and under emotion."}, {"t": 106.56, "txt": "Now let's get specific."}, {"t": 108.98, "txt": "When you break down thousands of blown accounts,"}, {"t": 111.6, "txt": "the same five patterns show up again and again."}, {"t": 115.02, "txt": "I call them the five account destroyers."}, {"t": 118.26, "txt": "And as we go through them, be honest with yourself,"}, {"t": 121.32, "txt": "because I promise you'll recognize at least one of them."}, {"t": 127.52, "txt": "Destroyer number one, trading without a plan."}, {"t": 131.22, "txt": "No written rules, no defined entry, no defined exit."}, {"t": 135.68, "txt": "Every single decision comes straight from gut feeling."}, {"t": 139.18, "txt": "And here's the problem with gut feeling in the market."}, {"t": 141.88, "txt": "Your gut was trained for survival, not for trading."}, {"t": 145.58, "txt": "It buys when things feel safe, which is usually the top."}, {"t": 149.26, "txt": "And it panics when things feel scary, which is usually the bottom."}, {"t": 153.72, "txt": "Destroyer number two, over trading."}, {"t": 157.06, "txt": "Taking 15 trades a day when there were maybe two good setups."}, {"t": 161.6, "txt": "Forcing entries out of boredom, just to feel like you're doing something."}, {"t": 165.66, "txt": "Every unnecessary trade costs you twice."}, {"t": 168.98, "txt": "Once in fees and spread and once in mental energy."}, {"t": 173.4, "txt": "The best traders I know are bored most of the day."}, {"t": 177.04, "txt": "That's not a bug, that's the job."}, {"t": 180.4, "txt": "Destroyer number three, risk that is far too high."}, {"t": 185.18, "txt": "Position sizes where one single trade decides the whole week."}, {"t": 189.78, "txt": "Maybe you know this feeling."}, {"t": 191.74, "txt": "One loss and suddenly you need three winners just to get back to zero."}, {"t": 196.56, "txt": "That's how accounts die, not slowly, but in two or three oversized trades."}, {"t": 202.92, "txt": "An account can survive many small mistakes."}, {"t": 205.96, "txt": "It cannot survive one big one."}, {"t": 210.66, "txt": "Destroyer number four, unrealistic expectations,"}, {"t": 215.16, "txt": "zero patience and the endless hunt for the holy grail."}, {"t": 219.02, "txt": "That one secret indicator, that one strategy with 95% win rate."}, {"t": 224.76, "txt": "Let me save you years, it does not exist."}, {"t": 228.48, "txt": "Every profitable trader you admire is running a system with losing trades in it."}, {"t": 233.62, "txt": "The difference is, their system survives the losers."}, {"t": 237.96, "txt": "And Destroyer number five, strategy hopping."}, {"t": 241.78, "txt": "Trying a strategy for one week, taking three losses and jumping to the next YouTube video."}, {"t": 247.76, "txt": "You never give any approach enough time to prove itself,"}, {"t": 250.7, "txt": "so you never collect real data about anything."}, {"t": 253.82, "txt": "It's like digging 10 wells two meters deep, instead of one well 20 meters deep."}, {"t": 259.4, "txt": "You do a lot of work and never hit water."}, {"t": 262.96, "txt": "Put all five together and you get the simple truth."}, {"t": 266.62, "txt": "Beginners lose money because they trade without a system."}, {"t": 272.56, "txt": "But there's a layer underneath those five mistakes."}, {"t": 276.12, "txt": "And it's the real engine behind all of them."}, {"t": 279.44, "txt": "Emotions."}, {"t": 280.84, "txt": "Three of them do most of the damage."}, {"t": 283.68, "txt": "Fear makes you close winning trades way too early."}, {"t": 287.28, "txt": "You take 20 pips of a 200 pip move just to feel safe."}, {"t": 292.0, "txt": "And it makes you skip perfectly good setups after two losses in a row."}, {"t": 296.6, "txt": "Greed does the opposite."}, {"t": 298.48, "txt": "It whispers double the size."}, {"t": 300.62, "txt": "This one is certain."}, {"t": 302.38, "txt": "And suddenly you're breaking your own rules on the most obvious trade of the week."}, {"t": 307.2, "txt": "And hope?"}, {"t": 308.92, "txt": "Hope is the most expensive one."}, {"t": 311.34, "txt": "Hope lets losses run because it will come back."}, {"t": 315.22, "txt": "Hope holds a bias for days after the market has already proven it wrong."}, {"t": 322.02, "txt": "And these three don't act alone."}, {"t": 324.84, "txt": "They feed a loop."}, {"t": 326.76, "txt": "Watch the chain."}, {"t": 328.22, "txt": "Emotions lead to bad decisions."}, {"t": 330.5, "txt": "Bad decisions lead to broken rules."}, {"t": 333.32, "txt": "Broken rules lead to losses."}, {"t": 336.32, "txt": "And every loss produces even more emotion."}, {"t": 340.54, "txt": "More fear."}, {"t": 341.6, "txt": "More greed."}, {"t": 342.76, "txt": "More hope."}, {"t": 344.16, "txt": "Round and round it goes."}, {"t": 346.42, "txt": "And with every lap the account gets smaller and the decisions get worse."}, {"t": 352.7, "txt": "This loop right here is what actually empties trading accounts."}, {"t": 357.86, "txt": "Not the market."}, {"t": 359.58, "txt": "The loop."}, {"t": 362.36, "txt": "On top of all that, there are four quiet account killers that nobody talks about"}, {"t": 367.22, "txt": "because they don't feel like mistakes while you're making them."}, {"t": 371.52, "txt": "First, information overload."}, {"t": 374.28, "txt": "20 strategies, 50 opinions, 5 gurus who all contradict each other."}, {"t": 379.78, "txt": "And you end up trading a random mix of everything and mastering nothing."}, {"t": 384.5, "txt": "Second, lack of real practice."}, {"t": 387.78, "txt": "Watching 100 hours of videos feels like progress, but knowledge is not skill."}, {"t": 392.96, "txt": "Nobody learns to swim from a book."}, {"t": 395.48, "txt": "Third, no feedback."}, {"t": 398.42, "txt": "You make the same mistake for six months and never notice"}, {"t": 401.3, "txt": "because nobody is looking over your shoulder and your journal is empty."}, {"t": 406.44, "txt": "And fourth, marketing instead of reality."}, {"t": 410.02, "txt": "Lambos, beach clips, 10,000 a month with one hour a day."}, {"t": 414.92, "txt": "That's a sales pitch, not a career plan."}, {"t": 418.12, "txt": "If you build your expectations on marketing, the real market will feel like a scam."}, {"t": 423.1, "txt": "It isn't."}, {"t": 424.18, "txt": "It's just real."}, {"t": 427.88, "txt": "So let me give you the actual formula, the honest one, without shortcuts."}, {"t": 433.52, "txt": "Profitability equals knowledge plus experience plus discipline plus execution."}, {"t": 441.42, "txt": "Look at that equation again."}, {"t": 443.92, "txt": "Knowledge is only one of the four terms."}, {"t": 447.46, "txt": "That's why watching more videos alone never made anyone profitable."}, {"t": 452.46, "txt": "Experience you collect in the market."}, {"t": 455.26, "txt": "Discipline you build by following rules when it hurts."}, {"t": 459.0, "txt": "And execution is doing the right thing on a Tuesday afternoon when nobody is watching."}, {"t": 465.02, "txt": "The good news?"}, {"t": 466.76, "txt": "Every single term is trainable."}, {"t": 471.48, "txt": "So here's the bottom line of this lesson."}, {"t": 474.26, "txt": "And it's the mindset shift that separates the 10% from the 90."}, {"t": 479.82, "txt": "Successful traders focus on the process, not on a single trade."}, {"t": 485.42, "txt": "One trade means nothing."}, {"t": 487.7, "txt": "It's noise."}, {"t": 489.0, "txt": "A hundred trades executed by the same clean system."}, {"t": 492.98, "txt": "That's a business."}, {"t": 495.24, "txt": "Build the system."}, {"t": 496.46, "txt": "Follow the system."}, {"t": 497.82, "txt": "Review the system."}, {"t": 499.66, "txt": "Do that and the results stop being luck and start being math."}, {"t": 505.42, "txt": "In the next lesson, we begin building exactly that system."}, {"t": 509.66, "txt": "Starting with the question, what is retail money?"}, {"t": 513.78, "txt": "And why does the market know exactly where it sits?"}, {"t": 517.12, "txt": "See you there."}]}